  "notes": "Drawn from a 2025 side-on photo of the left side (A321ceo). Right side not checked: the Arabic title may sit on the other side of the English there. The gray dots are a fine halftone of light gray dots on white, given as one flat light gray. Belly not seen: the red sweep and gray cone are taken to wrap underneath. Air Arabia Abu Dhabi, Egypt and Maroc fly the same scheme with their own small titles. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on A6-ATJ: 'AirArabia' runs x 0.154 to 0.341 as drawn (lowercase 0.74 of the A); the Arabic name x 0.346 to 0.409. The red sweep, the dotted cone and the fin's swoosh and panel are curves: smooth. Measured on the A321; Air Arabia's commonest type is the A320, where the titles sit the same distance behind the forward door.",
  "history": "Replaced Skyarium v1's approximation. Introduced 2020, replacing the earlier white scheme with the red/green/gray stripes and the bird on the fin."
}
